# FeatureStore-first

Canonical: [`docs/features.md`](../../docs/features.md) · [`docs/lessons.md#features`](../../docs/lessons.md#features) · [`docs/usage.md`](../../docs/usage.md)

## Rule

- **All** strategy/backtest features are read from **FeatureStore** (`feature_store_strict=True`).
- **Do not** add local `compute_*` fallbacks in backtest/diagnostic paths when a column is missing.
- Missing column → **backfill/build FS**, then re-run.

## When `features.yaml` gains a new `*_f`

1. Register in `config/feature_dependencies.yaml` (if not already).
2. **Incremental backfill** into the existing layer (do not rename layer unless intentional):

```bash
PYTHONPATH=src python scripts/build_feature_store_from_config.py \
  --config config/strategies/<archetype> \
  --symbols BTCUSDT,BNBUSDT,SOLUSDT \
  --timeframe 120T \
  --root feature_store \
  --layer features_<archetype>_<TF>_<hash> \
  --data-path data/parquet_data
```

- Builder detects missing output columns per month and runs **merge_mode** incremental (`+N features` only).
- Close-only features are fast to backfill. Demo pack: `config/strategies/ma_cross`.

## Anti-pattern

- Removing a feature from `requested_features` to dodge strict read errors.
- `_compute_*_column()` in backtest hot path when FS is configured.
